# Deny everything, then re-admit the directories the two images actually need. An allowlist rather
# than a list of exclusions, because the expensive things here — node_modules, coverage,
# playwright-report, test-results — are exactly the ones somebody forgets to add to a denylist.
#
# Neither image contains a build step, so the source tree is not part of the context at all:
# `dist/` and `dist-injector/` are produced by `npm run build` before either image is built. See
# the header of each Dockerfile.
*
!dist
!dist-injector
!docker
